SAM2 training data versioning (Synology, BTRFS)
================================================

Layout (all on the same BTRFS volume, /volume1/Data):

  /volume1/Data/Volumes/<VOLUME_NAME>/AnnotationCrops     live export (source)
  /volume1/Data/SAM2TrainingData/<vN>/<VOLUME_NAME>       frozen training versions

Each version is a copy-on-write (reflink) copy of the previous one with only the changed
files rewritten. Unchanged files share disk blocks with older versions, so a new version
costs roughly the size of what changed.

Scripts (run ON the NAS, over ssh)
----------------------------------

  version-bump <v-previous> <v-next>
      Reflink-clones SAM2TrainingData/<v-previous> to SAM2TrainingData/<v-next>.
      Refuses if <v-next> exists unless -f, which deletes <v-next> and re-clones it
      (anything only in <v-next> is lost). -n for dry run.

  version-sync [-n] [-d] [-j N] <version> [VOLUME_NAME ...]
      rsync from Volumes/<VOL>/AnnotationCrops into SAM2TrainingData/<version>/<VOL>,
      writing only files whose bytes differ (checksum, not timestamp). Default is all
      volumes already in <version>. Work is split into one rsync job per top-level subfolder of each volume, run in parallel (-j N sets the job count; default is the number of CPUs; -j 1 is sequential). -n lists changes only. -d deletes files from <version>
      that were removed from the source (otherwise they are kept).
      A volume not present in <v-previous> can be added by naming it explicitly.

  version-flatten [-n] <version> [VOLUME_NAME ...]
      For volumes stored as <version>/<VOL>/AnnotationCrops/<stuff>: moves <stuff> up into
      <VOL>/ and removes AnnotationCrops. Renames only (keeps shared blocks). Skips a
      volume on name collisions. version-sync refuses to run on such a volume.

Typical workflow
----------------

  version-bump v2 v3
  version-sync -n v3          # preview
  version-sync v3             # apply

Never run version-sync on an older version you want to keep frozen; bump first.

Install
-------

  mkdir -p ~/bin
  cp version-bump version-sync version-flatten ~/bin/ && chmod +x ~/bin/version-*
  echo 'export PATH="$HOME/bin:$PATH"' >> ~/.profile && . ~/.profile

DSM notes: ~/.profile needs the user home service enabled (Control Panel > User & Group >
Advanced). It is read only by interactive ssh logins; in Task Scheduler or `ssh nas 'cmd'`
use the full path. Paths can be overridden with DATA_ROOT / TRAIN_ROOT environment
variables.

Checking space
--------------

  df -h /volume1                                  # Used should barely move after version-bump
  btrfs filesystem du -s /volume1/Data/SAM2TrainingData/v3/<VOL>
      Exclusive = bytes unique to v3 (about the size of the changed files)
      Set shared = bytes shared with other versions/the source

Caveats
-------

- Paths are case-sensitive on the NAS (SAM2TrainingData). Windows/SMB hides this; make
  sure the real folder name matches.
- version-sync -c reads every file that exists in both places with the same size, so it
  is disk-bound on large volumes. Files with different sizes are detected without hashing.
- Reflinks only work within one BTRFS volume. Copying across volumes, or over SMB from
  Windows, makes full copies.
- Snapshots/Hyper Backup/replication of shared folders may not preserve block sharing on
  the target. Check the target's usage before relying on it.
